- No. Guys don't look at me like that.
- That's shocking.

474
00:27:33.800 --> 00:27:38.283
Absolutely, guys look at you like that.
I just saw two guys look at you like that.

475
00:27:38.360 --> 00:27:40.647
Erik Wolff and Cody Dennis
were 100% hitting on you.

476
00:27:40.760 --> 00:27:42.762
- We were just talking.
- A hundred percent.

477
00:27:42.840 --> 00:27:44.763
- There was absolutely no way-
- Yes, they were.

478
00:27:44.840 --> 00:27:46.763
Why don't you think
they were hitting on you?

479
00:27:46.840 --> 00:27:49.127
- Because I'm just... They weren't.
- Because you're what?

480
00:27:49.200 --> 00:27:51.646
- You're absolutely beautiful.
- Oh, my God. No!

481
00:28:33.880 --> 00:28:36.087
<i>Of course you're going to the prom.</i>

482
00:28:39.800 --> 00:28:42.041
<i>I'll take you.</i>

483
00:28:42.120 --> 00:28:44.122
Please go to the prom with me, Aimee!

484
00:28:47.640 --> 00:28:49.165
Yes.

485
00:28:50.800 --> 00:28:52.643
<i>You're taking her to prom?</i>

486
00:28:52.720 --> 00:28:54.927
Yeah. It's no big deal.

487
00:28:55.000 --> 00:28:58.004
It's you making plans, Sutter.
It's kind of a big deal.

488
00:28:58.080 --> 00:29:02.369
Relax. I'm just trying
to help this girl out.

489
00:29:02.440 --> 00:29:05.171
- Right. I forgot. Sutter to the rescue.
- Exactly!

490
00:29:08.680 --> 00:29:11.809
And if she falls for you,
what happens then?

491
00:29:14.120 --> 00:29:15.724
Shut up!

492
00:29:17.160 --> 00:29:18.969
Are you kidding me?

493
00:29:22.800 --> 00:29:25.371
<i>Hey, Sutter. It's Aimee.</i>

494
00:29:25.440 --> 00:29:28.250
<i>I didn't know if we were
gonna study today or not...</i>

495
00:29:28.320 --> 00:29:31.403
<i>but I hadn't heard from you, so-</i>

496
00:29:31.480 --> 00:29:33.164
<i>Yeah, yesterday-</i>

497
00:29:34.160 --> 00:29:36.640
<i>I had a really great time with you.</i>

498
00:29:37.680 --> 00:29:39.250
<i>Thank you.</i>

499
00:29:40.720 --> 00:29:43.087
<i>I'll talk to you later. Bye.</i>

500
00:30:11.560 --> 00:30:13.289
Or the lightning storm.

501
00:30:15.360 --> 00:30:16.850
On the roof.

502
00:30:17.840 --> 00:30:19.763
That was amazing.

503
00:30:19.880 --> 00:30:23.123
I've never felt like that with anyone.

504
00:30:23.200 --> 00:30:25.123
It's not very often.

505
00:30:25.200 --> 00:30:26.929
Except with you.

506
00:30:28.080 --> 00:30:30.765
Actually, I think
I'm feeling it right now.

507
00:30:30.840 --> 00:30:32.285
I'm feeling a moment right now.

508
00:30:32.360 --> 00:30:34.442
- Stop it.
- What? Cass, look. Seriously.

509
00:30:34.560 --> 00:30:38.281
When we're together,
it's like we're invincible or something.

510
00:30:38.360 --> 00:30:42.570
All this shit-the responsibilities,
all the problems, that stuff-

511
00:30:42.640 --> 00:30:44.961
that just disappears
when I'm with you.

512
00:30:45.040 --> 00:30:48.726
But you can't just have fun all the time.
You have to be serious.

513
00:30:48.800 --> 00:30:50.882
Hey, I'm 100% serious.

514
00:30:50.960 --> 00:30:54.009
- About what?
- About not being serious.

515
00:30:57.240 --> 00:30:59.322
Did you even apply to college yet?

516
00:30:59.400 --> 00:31:01.528
I don't need college.
Who needs that shit?

517
00:31:01.600 --> 00:31:04.285
Look, it's not-
I got everything I need right here.

518
00:31:04.360 --> 00:31:06.124
I've got a job, I've got a car...

519
00:31:06.200 --> 00:31:08.521
I've got a beautiful girl
sitting next to me.

520
00:31:08.600 --> 00:31:11.843
You think beauty's in some classroom
or some textbook, and it's not.

521
00:31:11.920 --> 00:31:14.491
That's not what it's about.
This right here.

522
00:31:14.600 --> 00:31:17.046
This is beautiful. All of this.

523
00:31:18.360 --> 00:31:20.362
That's all you need.

524
00:31:22.880 --> 00:31:24.689
You're drunk.

525
00:31:24.760 --> 00:31:27.001
I'm drunk?
Whatever! You're drunk!

526
00:31:27.080 --> 00:31:28.844
It doesn't matter.

527
00:31:28.920 --> 00:31:31.844
Okay, whatever.
I'm right-You're right.

528
00:31:31.920 --> 00:31:34.048
I'm just saying,
you gotta live in the moment.

529
00:31:34.160 --> 00:31:35.685
The moment?

530
00:31:38.480 --> 00:31:43.042
I want-
I want more than a moment.

531
00:31:43.120 --> 00:31:45.122
- I want-
- What?

532
00:31:46.880 --> 00:31:48.962
I want a future.

533
00:31:59.120 --> 00:32:01.248
And you can't do that.

534
00:32:04.600 --> 00:32:06.125
Wow.

535
00:32:09.160 --> 00:32:10.764
Wow.

536
00:32:18.400 --> 00:32:19.925
Please just go, Sutter.

537
00:32:20.040 --> 00:32:22.486
- Don't.
- Please just go.

538
00:32:24.280 --> 00:32:25.770
All right.

539
00:32:45.520 --> 00:32:47.522
What's up with you and Cassidy?

540
00:32:47.600 --> 00:32:49.887
- I don't want any trouble.
- Tell me the truth.

541
00:32:51.120 --> 00:32:52.770
Nothing's up, man.

542
00:32:52.840 --> 00:32:54.763
She's moved on.
I've moved on.

543
00:32:54.840 --> 00:32:57.002
- You've moved on?
- We hang out, and we have-

544
00:32:57.120 --> 00:32:58.849
Okay! Come on.

545
00:32:58.920 --> 00:33:01.161
We have fun,
but there's nothing going on.

546
00:33:01.240 --> 00:33:02.844
I promise you.

547
00:33:13.840 --> 00:33:16.764
- Can I ask you something?
- Yeah.

548
00:33:16.840 --> 00:33:19.844
Why can't it be me
that she has fun with?

549
00:33:19.920 --> 00:33:22.844
- What?
- Why can't it be me that she has fun with?

550
00:33:22.920 --> 00:33:25.571
I'm not like you.
I don't know how to make her laugh.

551
00:33:25.640 --> 00:33:28.041
Dude, you are Marcus West, man.

552
00:33:28.120 --> 00:33:29.690
You're the star athlete.

553
00:33:29.760 --> 00:33:32.001
You're the class president.
You are awesome!

554
00:33:32.080 --> 00:33:34.560
What's the name of that charity
that you started?

555
00:33:34.640 --> 00:33:36.005
The Hope Squadron.

556
00:33:36.080 --> 00:33:38.811
The fucking Hope Squadron, man!
That is awesome!

557
00:33:38.880 --> 00:33:41.281
You do not need my help.
You're the man.

558
00:33:41.360 --> 00:33:45.126
No, it's not the same.
The way she talks about you, man.

559
00:33:45.200 --> 00:33:47.601
I want her to like me like that,
and she doesn't.

560
00:33:47.680 --> 00:33:49.921
Trust me.
You don't want to be like me.

561
00:33:50.760 --> 00:33:54.765
I make jokes, yeah.
But, I mean, you get shit done.

562
00:33:54.840 --> 00:33:56.729
You're gonna change the world.

563
00:33:56.800 --> 00:33:59.121
You and Cass are perfect together.
Trust me.

564
00:33:59.200 --> 00:34:01.680
You're just too tense, man.
A little tense.

565
00:34:01.760 --> 00:34:04.889
- You gotta loosen up. You know?
- Yeah. Maybe.

566
00:34:04.960 --> 00:34:07.201
- Not everything has to be so serious.
- Yeah.

567
00:34:07.280 --> 00:34:09.760
I'm just saying you can relax.
You know?

568
00:34:09.840 --> 00:34:12.525
You're awesome.
Enjoy being who you are.

569
00:34:12.600 --> 00:34:14.921
Live in the now.
Embrace that shit.

570
00:34:15.680 --> 00:34:17.205
Yeah.

571
00:34:18.760 --> 00:34:20.603
Hey, thanks for-

572
00:34:20.680 --> 00:34:22.728
Thanks for talking to me like this.
I appreciate it.

573
00:34:22.800 --> 00:34:25.451
- Absolutely, man. It's a pleasure.
- I appreciate it. I really do.

574
00:34:25.520 --> 00:34:27.568
- Anytime.
- Sorry about the-

575
00:34:27.640 --> 00:34:29.881
it's cool. Good.

576
00:34:39.280 --> 00:34:42.011
- They're wrong about you.
- What's that?

577
00:34:42.880 --> 00:34:45.121
You're not the joke
everyone thinks, man.

578
00:35:02.040 --> 00:35:03.565
<i>Who do you think you are?</i>

579
00:35:03.640 --> 00:35:05.165
The king of Mexico?

580
00:35:05.240 --> 00:35:07.163
You're not gonna jerk
your way out of this.

581
00:35:07.240 --> 00:35:09.925
Aimee told me about
your little party by the lake.

582
00:35:10.000 --> 00:35:12.128
- And?
- And now you're avoiding her.

583
00:35:12.200 --> 00:35:14.089
- I'm not avoiding her.
- Really?

584
00:35:14.160 --> 00:35:16.401
Have you seen her since the party?
Have you even called?

585
00:35:16.480 --> 00:35:20.087
Why don't you get off my back
a little bit, give me some space.

586
00:35:20.160 --> 00:35:22.811
I knew she got that from you.
She said the exact same thing.

587
00:35:22.880 --> 00:35:25.406
- Good. Good for her.
- No, it's not good for her.

588
00:35:25.480 --> 00:35:27.528
Aimee isn't like you.
She's a sweet girl.

589
00:35:27.600 --> 00:35:29.648
She doesn't need you
causing problems in her life.

590
00:35:29.720 --> 00:35:31.051
What Aimee doesn't need...

591
00:35:31.120 --> 00:35:33.520
is you bossing her around
like she's your personal assistant.

592
00:35:34.480 --> 00:35:35.925
You shouldn't treat her this way.

593
00:35:36.000 --> 00:35:37.684
Thank you. Good talk.

594
00:36:00.800 --> 00:36:02.290
- Hi.
- Hey.

595
00:36:02.360 --> 00:36:04.442
- What's up?
- Nothing.

596
00:36:04.520 --> 00:36:07.046
What are you doing? I didn't know
you were coming over today.

597
00:36:07.120 --> 00:36:10.727
I wasn't planning on coming over,
but I was driving around and I thought...

598
00:36:10.800 --> 00:36:14.009
I don't care how busy I am,
I should see what Aimee is doing.

599
00:36:14.080 --> 00:36:17.050
So, how are you doing, Aimee?

600
00:36:17.120 --> 00:36:20.010
I'm good. I'm really good.
How are you, Sutter?

601
00:36:20.080 --> 00:36:21.684
- I'm good.
- Good.

602
00:36:21.760 --> 00:36:23.285
Yeah. Hey, listen.

603
00:36:23.360 --> 00:36:26.330
My sister, she's having
this fancy dinner party for her friends...

604
00:36:26.400 --> 00:36:28.448
and she's making me go.

605
00:36:28.520 --> 00:36:31.603
- I didn't know you had a sister.
- Yeah. We're not really that close.

606
00:36:33.000 --> 00:36:35.082
But would you want to go with me?

607
00:36:35.160 --> 00:36:37.003
- To dinner?
- Yeah.

608
00:36:37.080 --> 00:36:39.242
- Yeah. Yeah, absolutely.
- Okay. Cool.

609
00:36:40.320 --> 00:36:42.004
Yeah. What time?

610
00:36:42.080 --> 00:36:44.367
- Ten minutes.
- Ten minutes from now?

611
00:36:44.440 --> 00:36:45.885
- Yeah.
- Okay.

612
00:36:55.720 --> 00:36:59.247
So then I go
back up to the table and I say...

613
00:36:59.360 --> 00:37:01.647
“Can I get you boys anything else?”

614
00:37:01.720 --> 00:37:03.802
And then he says-

615
00:37:03.880 --> 00:37:06.281
I'm gonna let you say it.
What did you say?

616
00:37:06.360 --> 00:37:09.125
I leaned back in my chair,
puffed my chest out and said...

617
00:37:09.200 --> 00:37:11.771
“You can give me
your number, gorgeous.”

618
00:37:11.840 --> 00:37:15.367
That's right. And I didn't even know
that he was a big, fancy lawyer.

619
00:37:15.440 --> 00:37:17.602
I just gave it to him anyway.

620
00:37:17.680 --> 00:37:20.524
And I am so glad that I did.

621
00:37:20.600 --> 00:37:23.285
And she hasn't worked
a day in her life since.

622
00:37:23.360 --> 00:37:25.044
He's right. That's true.

623
00:37:26.200 --> 00:37:29.647
Wow. You guys sure are
a breath of fresh air.

624
00:37:30.360 --> 00:37:31.850
Thank you, Sutter.

625
00:37:31.920 --> 00:37:34.207
It's rare to see
such a happy couple nowadays.

626
00:37:34.280 --> 00:37:36.362
I feel like everyone's getting divorced.

627
00:37:36.480 --> 00:37:38.482
Well, that's not true.

628
00:37:38.560 --> 00:37:41.040
Isn't it? Our parents.

629
00:37:41.120 --> 00:37:43.805
Aimee's parents.
Most of my friends' parents.

630
00:37:43.880 --> 00:37:46.281
- Kid's got a point.
- Thank you, Joe.

631
00:37:46.360 --> 00:37:47.850
Mine didn't.

632
00:37:47.920 --> 00:37:49.888
- I thought your parents were divorced.
- No.

633
00:37:49.960 --> 00:37:53.203
There you go, Sutter. See?
Not everything is doomed.

634
00:37:55.000 --> 00:37:56.525
My dad died.

635
00:37:56.600 --> 00:37:58.011
What?

636
00:38:00.720 --> 00:38:02.848
I am so sorry.

637
00:38:02.920 --> 00:38:05.321
No. It's okay.
It's not your fault.

638
00:38:05.400 --> 00:38:07.164
What happened?

639
00:38:07.240 --> 00:38:08.924
He was a really great guy.

640
00:38:09.000 --> 00:38:13.642
He just kind of had
a slight problem with painkillers mostly.

641
00:38:13.720 --> 00:38:15.324
Yeah.

642
00:38:16.760 --> 00:38:18.922
Kinda crazy.
He tried to stop a bunch of times.

643
00:38:19.000 --> 00:38:21.082
But my sister came home one day...

644
00:38:21.160 --> 00:38:23.766
and he was lying
on the kitchen ﬂoor...

645
00:38:23.840 --> 00:38:26.730
and she had to close his eyes
and everything.

646
00:38:26.800 --> 00:38:29.690
It was pretty... intense.

647
00:38:31.920 --> 00:38:35.367
Sorry.
That was... really dark.

648
00:38:36.080 --> 00:38:39.368
Anyway, that's just-
I know that my marriage will work.

649
00:38:39.440 --> 00:38:41.044
Oh, yeah?

650
00:38:41.120 --> 00:38:43.202
I've thought it all out.

651
00:38:43.280 --> 00:38:46.363
My husband and I
will both live on a horse ranch...

652
00:38:46.440 --> 00:38:49.489
and I will work for NASA.

653
00:38:49.560 --> 00:38:52.086
And he'll do something
completely different.

654
00:38:52.160 --> 00:38:54.640
So that we offset each other.
You know?

655
00:38:54.720 --> 00:38:56.449
We'll have some things in common...

656
00:38:56.560 --> 00:38:59.643
but then we'll also bring all these
different dimensions to the table...

657
00:38:59.720 --> 00:39:02.963
so that, you know,
life doesn't get boring.

658
00:39:04.240 --> 00:39:06.322
I know it's gonna work.

659
00:39:06.400 --> 00:39:08.448
Sounds like a dream.

660
00:39:09.920 --> 00:39:13.049
I think it's good to have dreams.
Don't you?

661
00:39:15.400 --> 00:39:16.731
Yeah.

662
00:39:18.960 --> 00:39:21.531
- To dreams.
- To dreams.

663
00:39:28.000 --> 00:39:30.002
- I wanna ask you something.
- Okay.

664
00:39:32.320 --> 00:39:34.402
Did you mean what you said at the party?

665
00:39:35.480 --> 00:39:37.084
What?

666
00:39:38.320 --> 00:39:40.766
- What?
- You know!

667
00:39:40.840 --> 00:39:42.330
- No, I don't.
- Yes.

668
00:39:42.440 --> 00:39:46.729
Like, the thing about the prom
or whatever.

669
00:39:47.840 --> 00:39:50.081
Yeah, of course I remember that.
Are you kidding me?

670
00:39:50.200 --> 00:39:52.202
How could I forget something like that?

671
00:39:52.280 --> 00:39:54.442
No, I just mean, like...

672
00:39:54.520 --> 00:39:59.128
if you'd changed your mind or you
didn't want to go, I'd totally get it.

673
00:39:59.200 --> 00:40:01.771
- What are you talking about?
- No, I just-

674
00:40:01.840 --> 00:40:05.049
I wouldn't have asked you to go
if I didn't want to go with you.

675
00:40:05.120 --> 00:40:07.441
- I know.
- I wouldn't-

676
00:40:07.520 --> 00:40:09.045
I wouldn't have.

677
00:40:10.120 --> 00:40:14.682
I'm just saying that I know people
change their minds.

678
00:40:14.760 --> 00:40:16.728
- It's not that big of a deal.
- Not me.

679
00:40:16.800 --> 00:40:20.885
And I'm totally okay with it
if you want to not' go.

680
00:40:20.960 --> 00:40:24.043
I would not have asked you
to go to the prom...

681
00:40:24.120 --> 00:40:27.203
if I didn't want
to go to the prom with you.

682
00:40:29.040 --> 00:40:30.883
- Really?
- Really.

683
00:40:35.320 --> 00:40:36.810
Come here.

684
00:40:37.480 --> 00:40:39.164
Come here.

685
00:40:46.080 --> 00:40:47.570
- Bye.
- Bye.

686
00:40:49.520 --> 00:40:52.569
What?
Look, man. It's under control.

687
00:40:52.640 --> 00:40:54.608
What's under control?

688
00:40:54.720 --> 00:40:58.327
Did it ever cross your mind
that maybe I'm attracted to that girl?

689
00:40:58.400 --> 00:41:00.323
No. No, not at all.

690
00:41:00.400 --> 00:41:03.210
Yeah, that's because
you haven't really looked at her.

691
00:41:03.280 --> 00:41:06.204
I'm telling you,
once you actually talk to her...

692
00:41:06.280 --> 00:41:08.248
you see who she is.

693
00:41:08.360 --> 00:41:10.567
I don't know, man.
She's really beautiful.

694
00:41:11.720 --> 00:41:13.722
“Beautiful”?
This isn't you, Sutter.

695
00:41:13.800 --> 00:41:15.768
- What, dude?
- You're gonna break her heart.

696
00:41:15.840 --> 00:41:20.482
Well, worst-case scenario, I'm just
giving her the boyfriend experience.

697
00:41:20.560 --> 00:41:23.769
That's worst-case scenario?
No way. No.

698
00:41:23.840 --> 00:41:26.241
Okay, well-I don't know.

699
00:41:26.320 --> 00:41:29.244
You and I both know a month, tops,
she'll be done with me.

700
00:41:29.320 --> 00:41:32.244
- Then she'll move on.
- Then if she doesn't, what happens?

701
00:41:32.320 --> 00:41:34.721
If she doesn't, that'll be a first.

702
00:41:44.840 --> 00:41:46.842
I like you so much.

703
00:41:47.720 --> 00:41:49.290
I like <i>you.</i>

704
00:41:52.560 --> 00:41:55.564
Should we take our shirts off?

705
00:41:57.040 --> 00:41:58.565
Yeah.

706
00:41:59.480 --> 00:42:01.323
You go first.

707
00:42:01.400 --> 00:42:02.890
All right.

708
00:42:09.640 --> 00:42:12.644
- Voilà.
- You're amazing.

709
00:42:14.640 --> 00:42:16.642
So amazing.

710
00:42:18.320 --> 00:42:20.004
Your turn.

711
00:42:20.080 --> 00:42:23.129
- I have to take mine off?
- Yeah.

712
00:42:23.200 --> 00:42:25.248
Don't laugh. Okay?

713
00:42:25.320 --> 00:42:27.448
Okay. I promise I won't laugh.

714
00:42:27.520 --> 00:42:29.488
- Wow.
- Stop. No. You promised.

715
00:42:29.560 --> 00:42:31.005
- What?
- Don't say anything.

716
00:42:31.080 --> 00:42:33.162
Are you kidding me?
That's awesome.

717
00:42:51.480 --> 00:42:53.050
I like you, Sutter...

718
00:42:53.960 --> 00:42:55.530
so much.

719
00:43:14.120 --> 00:43:16.805
Do you wanna do this?

720
00:43:16.880 --> 00:43:18.484
- Yeah.
- Okay.

721
00:43:20.000 --> 00:43:22.002
Do you? Yeah? Okay.

722
00:43:22.120 --> 00:43:23.610
Hold on.

723
00:43:27.560 --> 00:43:29.164
- Here.
- Wow.

724
00:43:29.240 --> 00:43:32.005
- Where did you even get this from?
- I don't know.

725
00:43:32.080 --> 00:43:35.402
It's better.
Good to be safe, huh?

726
00:43:36.560 --> 00:43:38.244
Got all your bases covered.

727
00:43:42.920 --> 00:43:45.002
You got it?

728
00:43:45.080 --> 00:43:46.969
- Yeah.
- Do you need any help?

729
00:43:47.040 --> 00:43:49.168
- No.
- Are you sure?

730
00:43:49.240 --> 00:43:51.163
You okay?

731
00:43:51.240 --> 00:43:53.242
- Yeah.
- Okay.

732
00:44:11.000 --> 00:44:12.445
- Oh, my gosh.
- What?

733
00:44:12.520 --> 00:44:13.885
Nothing.

734
00:44:13.960 --> 00:44:16.281
- You wanna do it?
- Yeah.

735
00:44:16.360 --> 00:44:18.124
- Hey.
- Yeah?

736
00:44:18.200 --> 00:44:20.202
I'm so glad that I met you.

737
00:44:21.400 --> 00:44:23.402
I'm so glad that I met you too.

738
00:44:36.560 --> 00:44:39.962
Go slow. Go really slow.

739
00:44:40.040 --> 00:44:41.565
Okay?

740
00:44:44.440 --> 00:44:45.930
- Sorry.
- Sorry.

741
00:44:46.000 --> 00:44:47.525
It's okay.

742
00:44:50.240 --> 00:44:52.242
- You okay?
- Yeah.

743
00:45:39.440 --> 00:45:41.363
Tell you a secret?

744
00:45:41.440 --> 00:45:43.010
What?

745
00:45:43.080 --> 00:45:46.129
- My dad's not a pilot.
- What?

746
00:45:46.200 --> 00:45:51.570
Yeah, I actually don't know
what my dad does or where he is.

747
00:45:52.320 --> 00:45:54.721
- What? Sutter.
- Yeah.

748
00:45:54.800 --> 00:45:59.249
I just made that up because
he's been gone for half my life and...

749
00:46:00.800 --> 00:46:02.484
I guess I just miss him.

750
00:46:02.560 --> 00:46:04.403
Oh, my God.

751
00:46:04.480 --> 00:46:06.482
No one knows where he is?

752
00:46:06.560 --> 00:46:10.326
My mom knows where he is,
but she won't tell me.

753
00:46:10.400 --> 00:46:11.606
- What?
- Yeah.

754
00:46:11.680 --> 00:46:14.081
She can't keep him from you.
He's your dad.

755
00:46:14.160 --> 00:46:16.288
I know. She does. She has.

756
00:46:16.360 --> 00:46:18.488
Sutter, that's not, like-

757
00:46:20.960 --> 00:46:22.325
What?

758
00:46:22.400 --> 00:46:24.004
Yeah.

759
00:46:26.720 --> 00:46:28.722
I'll make you a deal.

760
00:46:29.400 --> 00:46:32.688
I will stand up to my mom
if you'll stand up to yours.

761
00:46:36.720 --> 00:46:38.210
What do you think?

762
00:46:40.760 --> 00:46:42.524
I think...

763
00:46:42.600 --> 00:46:44.602
that you're wonderful.

764
00:46:50.320 --> 00:46:51.845
Can I look?

765
00:46:56.320 --> 00:46:58.766
- Sorry I didn't get you a limo.
- That's okay.

766
00:46:58.840 --> 00:47:00.968
But this...

767
00:47:01.800 --> 00:47:03.768
is my way of making it up to you.

768
00:47:03.880 --> 00:47:06.690
- You did not have to get me anything.
- I know. I wanted to.

769
00:47:07.720 --> 00:47:08.960
I wrapped it.

770
00:47:09.040 --> 00:47:10.530
- Should I open it?
- Yeah.

771
00:47:10.640 --> 00:47:12.130
- You wrapped this?
- In newspaper.

772
00:47:12.200 --> 00:47:15.283
- It's beautiful.
- Thank you. Took me forever.

773
00:47:15.360 --> 00:47:16.964
- Okay. Thank you.
- You're welcome.

774
00:47:17.040 --> 00:47:19.042
I don't know what it is, but thank you.

775
00:47:22.120 --> 00:47:25.010
- What?
- Yeah! I know. Do you like it?

776
00:47:25.840 --> 00:47:27.604
- I love it!
- Do you? All right. Good.

777
00:47:27.680 --> 00:47:29.682
- It has my name on it?
- Uh-huh.

778
00:47:31.720 --> 00:47:33.600
- Thank you.
- Glad you like it. You're welcome.

779
00:47:33.640 --> 00:47:37.326
- You did not need to do this.
- I know, but the best part is, it's full.

780
00:47:38.040 --> 00:47:40.088
- It <i>is</i> full.
- Yeah. Mostly.

781
00:47:40.160 --> 00:47:42.367
- Did you take a sip?
- I took a sip, made sure it worked.

782
00:47:42.440 --> 00:47:44.488
- For good luck?
- Yup.

783
00:47:44.560 --> 00:47:46.085
- Ready?
- Yeah.

784
00:47:46.160 --> 00:47:47.400
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

785
00:47:47.480 --> 00:47:50.086
- To you, Aimee Finecky.
- To you, Sutter Keely.

786
00:48:07.400 --> 00:48:10.688
Ricky! Looking good, brother.
Looking good.

787
00:48:14.800 --> 00:48:16.564
- For you.
- Thank you.

788
00:48:16.640 --> 00:48:18.165
My lady.

789
00:48:20.240 --> 00:48:21.730
So nice.

790
00:48:23.000 --> 00:48:25.002
- Want some?
- Yeah.

791
00:48:38.200 --> 00:48:40.202
- Okay?
- Yeah. Thank you.

792
00:48:44.040 --> 00:48:46.691
- She's a good dancer.
- Who?

793
00:48:46.760 --> 00:48:49.411
- Cassidy.
- I didn't notice.

794
00:48:51.280 --> 00:48:52.930
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

795
00:49:13.240 --> 00:49:14.765
Why aren't you guys dancing?

796
00:49:14.840 --> 00:49:17.844
- We're gonna get out there next song.
- Come on. It's prom.

797
00:49:17.920 --> 00:49:20.287
- Aimee, dance with me.
- No. I'm good.

798
00:49:20.360 --> 00:49:23.284
- I don't really dance.
- Lucky for you, I'm a phenomenal dancer.

799
00:49:23.360 --> 00:49:27.251
- I can teach you some stuff.
- No, I'm fine.

800
00:49:27.360 --> 00:49:29.010
You guys should go.

801
00:49:29.080 --> 00:49:32.163
- Are you sure?
- Yeah. Absolutely.

802
00:49:34.000 --> 00:49:35.604
All right. Good.

803
00:49:37.560 --> 00:49:39.085
Have fun.

804
00:49:44.400 --> 00:49:47.529
She looks very nice.
Have you turned her into a lush yet?

805
00:49:47.600 --> 00:49:50.331
Do you want to lecture me about it,
or you wanna dance?

806
00:49:50.400 --> 00:49:52.004
Okay. I wanna dance.

807
00:49:59.640 --> 00:50:02.041
Pump the arms.
Pump the arms.

808
00:50:02.120 --> 00:50:04.202
Yep. That's what we're doing.

809
00:50:15.640 --> 00:50:17.483
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

810
00:50:19.880 --> 00:50:21.882
God, this is awesome.

811
00:50:24.280 --> 00:50:27.648
Seriously, like,
everybody's just singin'...

812
00:50:27.720 --> 00:50:29.802
and dancing...

813
00:50:29.920 --> 00:50:31.922
and falling in love.

814
00:50:37.400 --> 00:50:39.209
I'm so happy.

815
00:50:39.280 --> 00:50:41.681
I mean, this, like-this is our night.

816
00:50:41.760 --> 00:50:44.366
This is the youngest
that we're ever gonna be.

817
00:50:52.520 --> 00:50:55.000
I love these people.

818
00:50:55.080 --> 00:50:57.765
I do. I love these people.
I love you all!

819
00:51:00.520 --> 00:51:04.241
Come on. Dance with me.
Come on.

820
00:51:22.760 --> 00:51:25.047
Sorry I don't know
how to dance like Cassidy.

821
00:51:25.120 --> 00:51:27.805
You dance like Aimee.
That's perfect.

822
00:51:45.680 --> 00:51:49.127
- Oh, my gosh.
- What?

823
00:51:49.200 --> 00:51:50.929
Guess what!

824
00:51:51.000 --> 00:51:52.729
My sister called me today...

825
00:51:52.800 --> 00:51:56.930
and she said that she could probably,
almost 100% likely...

826
00:51:57.000 --> 00:51:59.082
get me a job at the bookstore.

827
00:51:59.160 --> 00:52:00.605
- In Philadelphia?
- Yes!

828
00:52:00.720 --> 00:52:03.803
- That's awesome. You love books.
- I know! It's perfect.

829
00:52:03.880 --> 00:52:06.850
- That's the perfect job for you.
- It really is.

830
00:52:06.920 --> 00:52:11.482
It'll help pay for college, and-
Yeah.

831
00:52:11.560 --> 00:52:14.882
- You talk to your mom yet?
- No.

832
00:52:14.960 --> 00:52:18.851
But I will... eventually.

833
00:52:24.360 --> 00:52:25.850
It's pretty.

834
00:52:28.800 --> 00:52:30.768
Sorry.

835
00:52:30.840 --> 00:52:32.842
Come here. Sorry.

836
00:52:36.360 --> 00:52:37.885
So abusive.

837
00:52:39.120 --> 00:52:40.690
Sorry.

838
00:52:42.120 --> 00:52:44.441
Back to what I was saying.

839
00:52:44.520 --> 00:52:47.729
I have been thinking...

840
00:52:47.800 --> 00:52:50.087
a lot recently-

841
00:52:50.160 --> 00:52:52.640
a lot more than normal-

842
00:52:52.720 --> 00:52:55.803
and I think that you
should come with me.

843
00:52:56.960 --> 00:52:58.689
- To...
- Philly.

844
00:52:58.760 --> 00:53:01.445
- Philly.
- Yes. Yes!

845
00:53:01.520 --> 00:53:03.966
I've been looking all into it.

846
00:53:04.040 --> 00:53:07.010
And you can go to the junior college...

847
00:53:07.120 --> 00:53:10.488
and we could both get jobs downtown.

848
00:53:10.560 --> 00:53:12.847
It could be really awesome.

849
00:53:12.960 --> 00:53:15.964
Have you ever been to Philly?
Have you seen the Liberty Bell?

850
00:53:16.040 --> 00:53:19.203
- No.
- I haven't either, but-

851
00:53:19.280 --> 00:53:22.011
but the pictures of it
are really beautiful.

852
00:53:22.080 --> 00:53:24.082
It's awesome.

853
00:53:24.160 --> 00:53:26.845
You've been thinking about this
for a while, haven't you?

854
00:53:26.920 --> 00:53:29.321
I have. I have. Yeah.

855
00:53:29.400 --> 00:53:33.530
And the coolest thing ever, also,
when I was talking to my sister-

856
00:53:33.600 --> 00:53:36.968
- Besides the Liberty Bell?
- Yes. There's so many cool things!

857
00:53:37.040 --> 00:53:41.090
She said that there's, like,
tons of vacancies avail-

858
00:53:41.160 --> 00:53:43.527
- Listen to me. I'm talking.
- I'm listening.

859
00:53:43.600 --> 00:53:47.844
She said there's tons of vacancies
available in her building...

860
00:53:47.920 --> 00:53:50.890
because of the economy
and stuff, so-

861
00:53:50.960 --> 00:53:53.531
We could totally just move there...

862
00:53:53.600 --> 00:53:55.568
at the end of June, together.

863
00:53:55.640 --> 00:53:59.361
And it would be really inexpensive
and awesome and-

864
00:54:01.320 --> 00:54:03.049
What do you think?

865
00:54:04.960 --> 00:54:07.440
I think that's great.

866
00:54:07.520 --> 00:54:09.921
- Really?
- Yeah.

867
00:54:15.880 --> 00:54:17.803
I did it.

868
00:54:17.880 --> 00:54:20.486
- What?
- Talked to my mom.

869
00:54:21.480 --> 00:54:23.323
I walked in and said...

870
00:54:23.400 --> 00:54:25.880
“It's my life, and I'm not gonna
let you stand in the way of it.”

871
00:54:25.960 --> 00:54:28.406
- How'd that go?
- It was ugly at first.

872
00:54:28.480 --> 00:54:31.324
Said all these things
and tried to guilt me into staying...

873
00:54:31.400 --> 00:54:35.610
but I just said, “Look,
if I can afford it, then I'm leaving...

874
00:54:35.680 --> 00:54:38.490
and there's really not anything
you can do about it.”

875
00:54:38.560 --> 00:54:40.562
That's awesome.
I'm proud of you.

876
00:54:40.640 --> 00:54:42.563
Thank you.
I'm proud of me.

877
00:54:43.640 --> 00:54:45.563
It wasn't that bad.
You'll see.

878
00:54:45.640 --> 00:54:47.563
- What?
- When you do it.

879
00:54:47.680 --> 00:54:50.843
- What are you talking about?
- Sutter! We had a deal.

880
00:54:50.920 --> 00:54:53.890
Yeah. I don't know.

881
00:54:53.960 --> 00:54:56.930
What? You can totally do it.
Trust me.

882
00:54:57.000 --> 00:54:58.764
- Different.
- No.

883
00:54:58.840 --> 00:55:00.763
Okay, look. Repeat after me.

884
00:55:00.840 --> 00:55:04.606
Say, “I want to call my dad, Mom.
I want to motherfucking call him.”

885
00:55:06.000 --> 00:55:07.968
That's not fair.

886
00:55:12.680 --> 00:55:14.762
- What's wrong?
- Nothing.

887
00:55:14.840 --> 00:55:17.889
- Just wanted to ask you something.
- Okay. What is it?

888
00:55:18.000 --> 00:55:19.490
It's about Dad.

889
00:55:20.520 --> 00:55:23.251
- Oh, Sutter.
- I wanna talk to him.

890
00:55:23.320 --> 00:55:26.164
- I don't think that's a good idea.
- Why not?

891
00:55:27.440 --> 00:55:29.442
- He's my dad.
- And I'm your mom...

892
00:55:29.520 --> 00:55:31.682
and you live under my roof.

893
00:55:31.760 --> 00:55:33.762
I just wanna call him.

894
00:55:35.440 --> 00:55:39.525
This is my job. We can have
this conversation later. Okay?

895
00:55:41.120 --> 00:55:43.122
No wonder he left you.

896
00:55:58.920 --> 00:56:01.400
How do you like the landscaping
we did back here?

897
00:56:01.480 --> 00:56:04.324
Joe and I planted day lilies.
I don't know if you saw them.

898
00:56:04.400 --> 00:56:06.562
- Yeah, it looks really good.
- Really pretty.

899
00:56:07.280 --> 00:56:09.726
Hey, Holl, I was talking on the phone.

900
00:56:09.800 --> 00:56:11.802
I wanted to ask you about Dad.

901
00:56:11.880 --> 00:56:14.281
- You wanna dredge that up, huh?
- “Dredge”?

902
00:56:14.360 --> 00:56:18.046
Dad's not somebody that you dredge.
He's awesome.

903
00:56:19.400 --> 00:56:22.370
He used to tell us stories
in the tent in the backyard.

904
00:56:22.480 --> 00:56:24.960
- You remember that?
- I think that was mostly you.

905
00:56:25.040 --> 00:56:27.930
Do you remember when we
made that trip down to Mexico...

906
00:56:28.000 --> 00:56:30.890
and he had us going up to people
asking where the Belt Buckle Museum was?

907
00:56:30.960 --> 00:56:34.646
And why is there
no artichoke ice cream?

908
00:56:34.720 --> 00:56:37.246
That was hilarious!
Don't look at-

909
00:56:37.320 --> 00:56:39.607
- It was funny.
- It was embarrassing.

910
00:56:39.680 --> 00:56:42.286
No, it wasn't. It was funny.
People loved us.

911
00:56:43.120 --> 00:56:46.283
They loved you
because you were little and cute.

912
00:56:47.440 --> 00:56:49.761
The guys liked you.
They loved you.

913
00:56:49.840 --> 00:56:51.888
Thought you were
a hot little <i>muchacha.</i>

914
00:56:53.000 --> 00:56:54.764
- You liked it.
- Well...

915
00:56:54.840 --> 00:56:58.731
- Yeah. Uh-huh.
- He knew how to make friends at least.

916
00:56:58.800 --> 00:57:00.802
Damn right, he did.

917
00:57:03.160 --> 00:57:06.960
So, do you know what happened
between him and Mom?

918
00:57:07.040 --> 00:57:09.042
He cheated on her.

919
00:57:09.120 --> 00:57:11.964
Yeah, well, that's her version of it.

920
00:57:12.040 --> 00:57:13.644
And you think it's a lie?

921
00:57:13.720 --> 00:57:17.247
I don't think she's lying, but I think
there's two sides to every story.

922
00:57:17.320 --> 00:57:18.810
- Think about it.
- Sutter...

923
00:57:18.880 --> 00:57:21.645
She won't let us see him.
She won't even let us know where he is.

924
00:57:21.720 --> 00:57:24.007
Let's talk about something else.
How is your friend Aimee?

925
00:57:24.800 --> 00:57:26.802
You gotta admit it's a little suspicious.

926
00:57:26.920 --> 00:57:30.561
She won't even give me his phone number.
I can't talk to the guy.

927
00:57:32.760 --> 00:57:36.481
Every time that I ask her for his number,
she refuses to give it to me.

928
00:57:37.560 --> 00:57:40.245
Can you please ask her
for his number for me?

929
00:57:43.480 --> 00:57:44.970
Please.

930
00:57:45.920 --> 00:57:47.684
I don't have to ask her.

931
00:57:53.720 --> 00:57:56.041
- I know where he is.
- What?

932
00:58:27.120 --> 00:58:28.884
Thank you. Thanks.

933
00:58:33.320 --> 00:58:34.810
Thanks.

934
00:58:38.560 --> 00:58:40.164
Hey, Sutter?

935
00:58:41.880 --> 00:58:44.360
Come by for lunch sometime, okay?

936
00:58:45.560 --> 00:58:47.688
Okay. I will. Promise.

937
00:59:12.040 --> 00:59:13.565
<i>Hello.</i>

938
00:59:14.760 --> 00:59:16.000
Dad?

939
00:59:16.080 --> 00:59:18.082
<i>You got the wrong number.</i>

940
00:59:18.920 --> 00:59:21.400
No, it's me, Sutter.

941
00:59:21.480 --> 00:59:22.970
<i>Sutter?</i>

942
00:59:27.040 --> 00:59:28.883
<i>Sutter, how you doin'?</i>

943
00:59:29.000 --> 00:59:30.684
Yeah, I'm all right.

944
00:59:30.760 --> 00:59:34.970
<i>You sound like a man from here now.</i>

945
00:59:35.040 --> 00:59:38.567
<i>Well, yeah, you-
Hey, you still playing ball?</i>

946
00:59:38.640 --> 00:59:40.449
What?

947
00:59:40.520 --> 00:59:42.045
<i>I mean, your arm.</i>

948
00:59:42.120 --> 00:59:46.125
<i>You were small for your age,
but you were a hell of a pitcher.</i>

949
00:59:46.200 --> 00:59:47.725
<i>You still playing ball?</i>

950
00:59:48.560 --> 00:59:52.087
Wow. Yeah, I'm surprised
that you remember that, Dad.

951
00:59:53.160 --> 00:59:56.881
<i>What are you talking about?
Of course I remember that.</i>

952
00:59:56.960 --> 00:59:58.485
<i>You still throwing?</i>

953
00:59:58.560 --> 01:00:02.087
No, not really.
Haven't thrown much lately.

954
01:00:02.200 --> 01:00:05.841
<i>It's a shame. You were
a hell of a pitcher. You had a great arm.</i>

955
01:00:05.920 --> 01:00:08.002
<i>So, how...</i>

956
01:00:08.080 --> 01:00:12.369
<i>So how's your-
How's your mom and Holly doin'?</i>

957
01:00:12.440 --> 01:00:15.205
They're good.
Yeah, real good.

958
01:00:15.280 --> 01:00:19.410
<i>Good. That's tremendous, Son.
That's good. That's good.</i>

959
01:00:21.360 --> 01:00:22.964
Listen, Dad-

960
01:00:24.800 --> 01:00:27.929
Can I come see you sometime?

961
01:00:28.000 --> 01:00:30.651
<i>Come see me?
Of course you can come see me.</i>

962
01:00:30.720 --> 01:00:32.961
<i>What do you mean,
can you come see me?</i>

963
