Yeah, it's probably not cool.

1202
01:18:41.040 --> 01:18:43.407
Sorry. It's just-

1203
01:18:43.480 --> 01:18:45.608
- I'm...
- Hey, I get it. It's cool.

1204
01:18:45.680 --> 01:18:49.526
I'm trying to do things right now
that aren't bad for me.

1205
01:18:50.640 --> 01:18:52.324
I get it.

1206
01:18:53.160 --> 01:18:54.525
I get it.

1207
01:18:54.600 --> 01:18:56.602
It's cool. It's cool.

1208
01:19:08.120 --> 01:19:10.043
I'm not mad at you.

1209
01:19:10.120 --> 01:19:11.645
I know.

1210
01:19:16.360 --> 01:19:18.886
You'll always be
my favorite ex-boyfriend.

1211
01:19:36.320 --> 01:19:37.765
- Sutter.
- Yeah.

1212
01:19:37.840 --> 01:19:39.842
Pop upstairs, would ya?

1213
01:19:44.720 --> 01:19:48.281
You've probably noticed
we haven't been too busy these days.

1214
01:19:48.360 --> 01:19:51.967
And because of that,
I can only keep one clerk.

1215
01:19:54.080 --> 01:19:55.923
Now, I like you, Sutter...

1216
01:19:56.000 --> 01:19:59.163
but more importantly,
the customers like you...

1217
01:19:59.240 --> 01:20:02.608
so I think you should be the one I keep.

1218
01:20:02.680 --> 01:20:04.125
That's excellent.

1219
01:20:04.200 --> 01:20:06.009
One second.

1220
01:20:06.080 --> 01:20:10.768
I've given this some hard thought,
and the only way I can let you stay...

1221
01:20:10.840 --> 01:20:13.446
is if you promise me 100%...

1222
01:20:13.520 --> 01:20:16.842
that you will never
come in here loaded again.

1223
01:20:16.920 --> 01:20:21.005
And I'm serious.
Not even a light buzz.

1224
01:20:21.080 --> 01:20:25.130
Because if you do,
then I have to let you go.

1225
01:20:25.200 --> 01:20:26.690
You understand.

1226
01:20:27.520 --> 01:20:29.045
I do.

1227
01:20:31.040 --> 01:20:32.530
Can you promise?

1228
01:20:34.960 --> 01:20:37.088
You got me there, Dan.

1229
01:20:40.040 --> 01:20:42.042
You know I can't promise you that.

1230
01:20:46.400 --> 01:20:49.131
Well, I appreciate your honesty.

1231
01:20:50.960 --> 01:20:53.486
I've always been up front with you.

1232
01:21:00.160 --> 01:21:01.650
Thanks for the opportunity.

1233
01:21:01.720 --> 01:21:03.210
- Yeah.
- Thank you.

1234
01:21:03.280 --> 01:21:05.487
I suppose if I was your father...

1235
01:21:05.560 --> 01:21:08.484
this is where I might give you
a lecture or something...

1236
01:21:08.560 --> 01:21:11.643
about what you're doing to yourself.

1237
01:21:11.760 --> 01:21:14.411
If you were my dad,
you wouldn't have to.

1238
01:21:33.600 --> 01:21:36.922
<i>Bus 710 now boarding
for Washington, DC...</i>

1239
01:21:37.000 --> 01:21:39.002
<i>Baltimore and Philadelphia.</i>

1240
01:22:21.400 --> 01:22:23.528
Miss, I need to keep going.

1241
01:22:23.600 --> 01:22:25.728
Just two more minutes, please.
I promise.

1242
01:22:25.800 --> 01:22:28.167
I'm sorry.
I'm gonna have to go.

1243
01:22:28.240 --> 01:22:30.242
Okay. Thanks.

1244
01:22:56.600 --> 01:22:59.080
So, do you think I did the right thing?

1245
01:23:00.680 --> 01:23:02.682
For you, or for her?

1246
01:23:03.520 --> 01:23:07.445
You had to let her go.
You had to save that girl.

1247
01:23:07.520 --> 01:23:11.730
That's what I'm-
I saved her. I saved her.

1248
01:23:11.840 --> 01:23:13.365
You're not wrong.

1249
01:23:15.280 --> 01:23:18.966
You're a hero.
You're a king.

1250
01:23:19.040 --> 01:23:20.530
I'm a king.

1251
01:23:21.720 --> 01:23:23.722
I'm a king.

1252
01:23:23.800 --> 01:23:26.201
Look at you, Sutter.

1253
01:23:26.280 --> 01:23:29.284
What are you, 22, 23?

1254
01:23:29.400 --> 01:23:30.845
Yeah.

1255
01:23:30.920 --> 01:23:32.604
Beautiful.

1256
01:23:32.680 --> 01:23:35.490
You got your whole life ahead of you.

1257
01:23:35.560 --> 01:23:37.483
Hey, so do you, man.

1258
01:23:37.560 --> 01:23:40.404
- You think so?
- Absolutely.

1259
01:23:40.480 --> 01:23:42.562
Look at you. You're a young man.

1260
01:23:43.560 --> 01:23:45.085
You're a kid.

1261
01:23:45.160 --> 01:23:47.766
- I'm a kid?
- You got-

1262
01:23:47.840 --> 01:23:50.127
You got plenty of life left in you.

1263
01:23:50.200 --> 01:23:54.489
Hey. How 'bout we get a round of shots?

1264
01:23:54.560 --> 01:23:56.403
For us kids.

1265
01:24:37.800 --> 01:24:39.450
Oh, shit.

1266
01:24:42.080 --> 01:24:43.650
Oh, shit.

1267
01:24:45.360 --> 01:24:47.886
What the hell-Sutter?

1268
01:24:48.920 --> 01:24:50.843
Jesus Christ.
We just went through this.

1269
01:24:50.920 --> 01:24:53.764
- What the hell is wrong with you?
- What do you care?

1270
01:24:53.840 --> 01:24:57.925
- Excuse me?
- You've never cared about me.

1271
01:24:58.000 --> 01:25:01.129
Is it 'cause I remind you of him?
Is that why you hate me?

1272
01:25:01.240 --> 01:25:03.561
You can't even stand
to look at me, can you?

1273
01:25:03.640 --> 01:25:05.608
What are you talking about?
You're my son!

1274
01:25:05.680 --> 01:25:08.763
I'm his son too.
I'm exactly like him.

1275
01:25:09.600 --> 01:25:12.171
You are nothing like him.

1276
01:25:15.480 --> 01:25:18.404
I'll give you your dad's number,
and you can go to him and see.

1277
01:25:18.480 --> 01:25:21.450
- See how different you are.
- I thought you didn't want me to see him.

1278
01:25:21.520 --> 01:25:25.047
I was trying to protect you from-

1279
01:25:25.120 --> 01:25:28.408
I was wrong, okay?
So I want you to go now.

1280
01:25:28.480 --> 01:25:30.050
I already went.

1281
01:25:33.080 --> 01:25:37.244
Holly gave me his number.
I drove up there last week and I saw him.

1282
01:25:37.360 --> 01:25:39.362
You were right, Mom.

1283
01:25:41.080 --> 01:25:42.889
You were right the whole time.

1284
01:25:42.960 --> 01:25:44.962
You are not' your father.

1285
01:25:47.720 --> 01:25:49.404
Sutter, listen to me.

1286
01:25:50.400 --> 01:25:55.406
Listen to me. That man
has never loved anyone but himself.

1287
01:25:55.480 --> 01:25:57.881
His heart is this big.

1288
01:25:57.960 --> 01:26:01.123
But you love everybody.

1289
01:26:01.200 --> 01:26:03.851
You have the biggest heart
of anyone I know.

1290
01:26:04.960 --> 01:26:07.327
When you were in third grade,
and Ricky was on crutches-

1291
01:26:07.400 --> 01:26:10.449
Do you remember that?
You carried his books.

1292
01:26:10.560 --> 01:26:13.370
Carried that backpack every day.

1293
01:26:13.480 --> 01:26:16.802
And when you were nine
and Rosemary Clark lost her mother?

1294
01:26:16.880 --> 01:26:19.281
You invited her to come live with us.

1295
01:26:19.400 --> 01:26:22.563
You told her
that I would be her new mom.

1296
01:26:24.880 --> 01:26:27.042
You've always been so special, Sutter.

1297
01:26:28.120 --> 01:26:30.566
That's why everyone loves you so much.

1298
01:26:31.720 --> 01:26:33.722
Nobody loves me.

1299
01:26:36.640 --> 01:26:38.927
Sutter, you are so wrong.

1300
01:26:39.000 --> 01:26:41.082
Do you hear me?
You are so wrong.

1301
01:27:25.200 --> 01:27:27.851
<i>My name is Sutter Keely,
and I'm 18 years old.</i>

1302
01:27:29.040 --> 01:27:32.362
<i>Compared to other kids,
I haven't had that many hardships.</i>

1303
01:27:32.440 --> 01:27:35.125
<i>Not really.
You know, shit's happened.</i>

1304
01:27:36.120 --> 01:27:38.088
<i>Stuff has happened, sure.</i>

1305
01:27:38.160 --> 01:27:41.289
<i>But stuff always happens, right?</i>

1306
01:27:41.400 --> 01:27:45.485
<i>But the real challenge in my life,
the real hardship...</i>

1307
01:27:45.560 --> 01:27:47.050
<i>is me.</i>

1308
01:27:47.720 --> 01:27:49.290
<i>It's always been me.</i>

1309
01:27:50.280 --> 01:27:53.602
<i>As long as I can remember,
I've never not been afraid.</i>

1310
01:27:53.680 --> 01:27:55.250
<i>Afraid of failure...</i>

1311
01:27:56.400 --> 01:27:58.641
<i>of letting people down...</i>

1312
01:28:00.080 --> 01:28:02.048
<i>hurting people...</i>

1313
01:28:02.120 --> 01:28:03.610
<i>getting hurt.</i>

1314
01:28:05.360 --> 01:28:10.810
<i>Before, if! Kept my guard up and
focused on other things, other people...</i>

1315
01:28:10.880 --> 01:28:14.771
<i>if! Couldn't even feel it,
then no harm would come to me.</i>

1316
01:28:14.840 --> 01:28:16.330
<i>I screwed up.</i>

1317
01:28:16.400 --> 01:28:19.688
<i>Not only did I shut out the pain,
I shut out everything-</i>

1318
01:28:19.760 --> 01:28:21.808
<i>the good and the bad-</i>

1319
01:28:23.040 --> 01:28:25.486
<i>until there was nothing.</i>

1320
01:28:29.640 --> 01:28:31.608
<i>It's fine to just live in the now...</i>

1321
01:28:31.680 --> 01:28:35.366
<i>but the best part about now
is there's another one tomorrow.</i>

1322
01:28:36.360 --> 01:28:38.840
<i>And I'm gonna start making them count.</i>

1323
01:28:38.920 --> 01:28:41.287
<i>Sincerely, Sutter Keely.</i>

1324
01:28:54.640 --> 01:28:57.291
<i>P. S. I don 'z' know if this
was due a long time ago.</i>

1325
01:28:57.360 --> 01:29:00.489
<i>Probably was. That's fine.</i>

1326
01:29:00.560 --> 01:29:03.166
<i>May be too late for this essay.</i>

1327
01:29:03.240 --> 01:29:05.402
<i>It's not too late for me.</i>
